% CODA, bars 325-376 (c030: header renumbered from the v03 numbers 333-384; the finale thread reads these bar numbers).
% c041: 345-348 T's second phrase (A major, D5-B5) in Ob 1, dolce, not Cl 1: concert B5 is the A clarinet's written D6, where Adler (I PDF 210, Ex. VII-56)
%   puts the 'piercing, shrill' register, the only soft clarinet note above written C6 in the movement; F4-C6 is the oboe's 'warm, prominent, reedy and
%   poignant' range and the oboe is 'basically a lyrical instrument' (PDF 198). The oboe had no phrase of T; Dvorak 9/iii gives its E-major tune to Ob 1 (68-75).
% c035: 361 Fl 1 prints "1." (no label was reprinted after the shared rest).
% c022: iv6 at 331 (C-E-A over C, Phrygian approach to V; c022 called it 339 in v23 numbers) replaces the diminished triad C sharp-E-G (A-S PDF 167 Ex. 11-6c, 168): Vln I C-A, Cl 2, Bsn 2, Cb, Cbsn on C, Bsn 1 A; no G, so no C-major triad.
% 325-340 Più mosso: motive x as a stretto ostinato entering from the bottom (Vc 325, Vla 326, Vln II 327, Vln I 328), pp crescendo; the bass falls
%   E-D-C-B (329-332); theme A's head ff (333); Vln I and Fl 1 peak on B6 at 336, fff, the movement's only fff (the scherzo's highest note, a semitone under the finale's C7);
%   hemiola 337-338, E minor chord (339), general pause (340).
% 341-376 Meno mosso (tempo del Trio), T returns p in Hn 1 (341), Cl 1 (345), Vln I and Fl 1 (349), cadence 355.
%   c013: T's first half (341-348) is in A major, the tonicized IV that a late coda can carry (Aldwell-Schachter Unit 26 sec. 11, PDF 451-452);
%   its half cadence on E (348, V of A) is the pivot back to E (I), and T's second half (349-356) confirms E with ii-ii6-6/4-V-I.
% 357-360: Hn 1 sings the motto's chromatic tail on the fifth degree, B-A sharp-A-G sharp (E flat-D-D flat-C transposed),
%   over E - A sharp dim7 - A minor (iv, mixture) - E: a plagal close that ends on G sharp.
% 361-376: E major held pp, then only Hn 1 and Vln I on G sharp (the pitch that opened the scherzo, movement II's A flat) over a timpani roll (372-374)
%   and a last pizzicato E with the harp's harmonics (375); the finale takes that G sharp as A flat (Hn 1 A flat 4, Vln I A flat 5).

% c043: 353-356 the movement's last authentic cadence is expanded: the cadential 6/4 holds two bars (353-354; Vln I/Fl 1 G sharp 6-F sharp-E over B,
%   the 6-5-4 descent of the 6/4's upper voice, theme A's minim-two-quaver rhythm), V7 at 355, I at 356, so it is no longer a copy of the trio tune's
%   internal cadences (165-167, 181-183, 221-223). Aldwell-Schachter Unit 19 PDF 317-318 (expanding the cadential 6/4; Ex. 19-21, 19-22 Brahms at the end
%   of the Requiem), PDF 314-315 (6-5-4-3 above a held bass), PDF 307 (the accented 6/4 delays the expected arrival). No bar added. Violas 354 G sharp-E (6/4),
%   355 A-F sharp (V7; the inner 4th rises, Vln I's falls: PDF 317). Vc/Cb pizz. B 353 and 355, E 356; arco from 358 (Bsn 2 holds E at 357), so pizz.->arco keeps 4 beats.
% c042: 358-360 violas G4-E4-E4 (were G4-A4-G sharp 4): the augmented 2nd G-A sharp against Hn 1 opens to the 4th E-A instead of closing into
%   a unison on Hn 1's A4, so the motto tail's A and G sharp sound alone at their pitch (A-S PDF 375 Ex. 22-2, 377); harmony and Hn 1 unchanged.
% c028: 325-328 the ostinato entries stay pp until Vln I has entered (328); all strings cresc. from 328, mf at 329, ff at 333 (Adler II PDF 37: hold back for the event).
% c028: 336 fff in all parts: Vln I's B6 and the timpani roll are the movement's peak, above the ff of 72, 104-120, 300-320 and 333 (Adler II PDF 38-40, Tchaikovsky 4/i).
% c032: 329-332 Vln I in 10ths above the falling bass (G-F#-E-D#, with Cl 1 an octave lower), not in octaves with it; the E-B drone gives way
%   to chord tones at 331 (iv6: A-E) and 332 (V: B-F#) in Vc, Vla, Vln II, so no B sounds against the bass C before the bass reaches B (A-S Unit 17, PDF 267-269, 277-279).
% c034: 336-338 trombones, bass trombone and tuba rest under the B6 peak and re-enter fff on the tonic chord at 339 (Adler II PDF 150, Barber Sym. 1:
%   trombones and tuba left out of the bar of the high note so it is not made heavy; the low brass entrance on the last chord gives the finality).
% c034: 333-335 Cl 1 (E5) and the violas (E4) take theme A's head with Vln I/Fl 1 and Vln II/Ob 1 instead of sustaining E: the agile instruments
%   carry the figure in octaves while the brass sustain (Adler II PDF 154, Smetana; PDF 150-151, the octave tutti that summarises an idea).
% c036: Fl 1 p, not pp: its line climbs to A6, the flute's top fourth, where soft dynamics and intonation are hardest to control (Adler PDF 174, 186)
% c044: 349-356 Fl 1 rests: the soft last statement of T is Vln I alone on top (pp, up to A6 and G sharp 6) with Cl 1 doubling Vln II's lower octave, not Fl 1 p over
%   Vln I pp at pitch. Adler II PDF 162 (Brahms 3/i last chord: a soft high flute overpowers; easier with the strings on top and the winds an octave below),
%   PDF 164 (violins play softly on any note), PDF 165 (doublings at pitch lose both colours), PDF 170-171 (a recurring passage coloured differently each time).
% c044: 361 Fl 1's manual "1." removed: after the 20-bar rest the part combiner prints the label itself (it printed twice).
% c044: 339 Cl 2 G4 (was B4): its seventh A4 (336-338) falls to G with Tpt 1's (Adler II PDF 161-162, Schumann 1/i: all sevenths resolve downward).
% c050: 329 the woodwinds (Cl 1-2, B.cl, Bsn 1-2) enter p, not mf at the strings' level, and crescendo faster to the ff at 333; Cbsn p at 331
%   (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 127, amplification: while the first group makes the crescendo gradually, the second enters piano and reaches its crescendo more rapidly).
% c050: 357-360 Vln II G sharp 4-G 4-E 4-E 4 and violas (with Bsn 1) E4/G sharp 3-C sharp 4-C 4-B 3: each chromatic step of the plagal close (G sharp-G, C sharp-C) is made in one voice,
%   so Vln II's G sharp 4 no longer meets the violas' G4 in the next chord (false relation), and Bsn 1 no longer doubles Hn 1's A-G sharp in octaves (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 126-127).
%   Hn 1's motto tail and the harmony E - A sharp dim7 - iv6/4 - E are unchanged; 361-364 Vln II G sharp 4, violas B3 (exchanged with the old parts).
% c061: 354-355 the quaver E of the 6-5-4 descent is tied into the V7 bar and resolves to D sharp on beat 2: the trio's new V4-3 (tA.ily) at the end of
%   the expanded 6/4 (Aldwell-Schachter PDF 353-354 Ex. 21-11b, 6/4 into 4-3 as a cadence formula; PDF 361 sec. 21, a delayed resolution builds tension). Violas A-F sharp, no D sharp on beat 1.
codaFluteOne = { R2.*8 | e'''4-.\ff b''8-. b''-. e'''4-. | g'''2->( fis'''8 f'''8 | e'''4-.) b''8-. b''-. g'''4-. | b'''2.->\fff | a'''2-> fis'''4->~ | fis'''4 dis'''2-> | e'''4-> r4 r4 | R2. | R2.*8 | R2.*8 | R2.*4 | gis''2.\pp | gis''2.~ | gis''2.~ | gis''2 r4 | R2.*12 | }
