% c029: 338 Hn 1 keeps B: the seventh A is Tpt 1's alone in the brass (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 102; as c019 at 104/300).
% c039: 331-332 the horns enter pp/p and crescendo into the ff at 333 (Hn 3-4 E-A on iv6 at 331, D sharp-B on V at 332; Hn 1-2 B-F sharp at 332), so the brass
%   join the coda's crescendo instead of entering at ff (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 127, 130; Ex. 258, PDF 421-422: horns, trumpets and tuba enter pp cresc. before the arrival). Low brass still enter at 333.
